                <pb facs="0447" n="345" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg345"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">5727/177.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Netherlands Chargé to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Royal Legation of the Netherlands</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-02-13"><hi rendition="#italic">February 13,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 150.]</seg></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of State</hi>: In reply to the
                    department’s note of January 16, I have the honor to inclose a copy of the
                    Bulletin of the Laws of Kingdom of Holland, No. 76, 1896, in which will be found
                    the royal decree of May 4, 1896, concerning the general regulations of chambers
                    of commerce in the Netherlands.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. A. Royaards.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
